[{:db/id "q-88591/selection/115ad3b079b59c078de2da73023224dd4ffc5df598122ed760a5caa32b998d43" :answer/id #uuid "4341a4f4-22e7-5e46-9103-ba2e52eaa542" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}{x}^{3}\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-88591/selection/aad2fca297c6b38e17e666c1f9eb69a4cd71126fa6233dad1e326c7f57bba31f" :answer/id #uuid "e8ed1d6e-ff2e-5a98-915b-bb0d19345642" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{x}^{3}\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-88591/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "429f604a-2d0e-5639-b1e3-05045449a1c8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-88591/selection/f68e9e1281a7202f5e512387e1a98744b843fcc300984681b1758ecb3f524be2" :answer/id #uuid "7d732af2-2633-53a4-ab0d-eb2ed7133d53" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}{x}^{3}\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-88591/selection/f1959cbdbcb75161e159e60a4cf6b28fd4a45b48764de70c304f0e0b05bb3a08" :answer/id #uuid "8a0abe02-949b-563c-ab66-764529873670" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{x}^{3}\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-88591/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "a42e4e26-511f-5e89-99fb-5a2c86787204" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-88591/selection/115ad3b079b59c078de2da73023224dd4ffc5df598122ed760a5caa32b998d43" :answer-field/choices ["q-88591/selection/115ad3b079b59c078de2da73023224dd4ffc5df598122ed760a5caa32b998d43" "q-88591/selection/aad2fca297c6b38e17e666c1f9eb69a4cd71126fa6233dad1e326c7f57bba31f" "q-88591/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" "q-88591/selection/f68e9e1281a7202f5e512387e1a98744b843fcc300984681b1758ecb3f524be2" "q-88591/selection/f1959cbdbcb75161e159e60a4cf6b28fd4a45b48764de70c304f0e0b05bb3a08"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-88591" :question/id #uuid "64adcc49-a78d-5de5-9601-bc19735c1f25" :question/math-academy-id "q-88591" :question/problem "Simplify the integral ${\\int }_{-\\pi /4}^{\\pi /4}{x}^{3}\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x$ using symmetry." :question/worked-solution "Recall the following:\n\n- a function $f(x)$ is *even* if $f(-x)=f(x)$\n\n- a function $f(x)$ is *odd* if $f(-x)=-f(x)$\n\nMoreover, for any even function $f(x),$ the graph of $y=f(x)$ is symmetric across the $y$-axis, so we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-a}^{a}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=2{\\int }_{0}^{a}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nNotice that $f(x)={x}^{3}\\operatorname{tan}⁡x$ is an even function. Indeed, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-x) & =(-x)^{3}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(-x) \\\\  & =-{x}^{3}(-\\operatorname{tan}⁡x) \\\\  & ={x}^{3}\\operatorname{tan}⁡x \\\\  & =f(x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, because $f(x)={x}^{3}\\operatorname{tan}⁡x$ is an even function, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-\\pi /4}^{\\pi /4}{x}^{3}\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=2{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}{x}^{3}\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-88591/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2688742c-1655-557a-888d-af7e2179a89c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-88591"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-88207"] :question/problem "Simplify the integral ${\\int }_{-7}^{7}3{x}^{6}\\,\\text{d}x$ using symmetry." :question/worked-solution "Recall the following:\n\n- a function $f(x)$ is *even* if $f(-x)=f(x)$\n\n- a function $f(x)$ is *odd* if $f(-x)=-f(x)$\n\nMoreover, for any even function $f(x),$ the graph of $y=f(x)$ is symmetric across the $y$-axis, so we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-a}^{a}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=2{\\int }_{0}^{a}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nNotice that $f(x)=3{x}^{6}$ is an even function. Indeed, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-x) & =3(-x)^{6} \\\\  & =3{x}^{6} \\\\  & =f(x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, because $f(x)=3{x}^{6}$ is an even function, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-7}^{7}3{x}^{6}\\,\\text{d}x=2{\\int }_{0}^{7}3{x}^{6}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-88586/selection/460d48d00f6d19174ffa7a6d5bddd5adc2a1dd496830c54e0b41a0757ee86cad" :answer/id #uuid "b35badc9-cc23-5c66-9272-b4414dcf6b27" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{10}{x}^{4}\\,{e}^{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-88586/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "49e824a2-8c83-5e2f-bdbc-b7b2b279f394" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-88586/selection/d792654b44e68206c78ac4117abf07436eb5fad4aeedd5e393f659f1be21a56f" :answer/id #uuid "65df433c-f9c4-5d0d-9dba-a073e32a8e83" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{\\int }_{0}^{5}{x}^{4}\\,{e}^{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-88586/selection/129db039b7a10bb7c3f543c25e49869593eb89b9f23cc8eb06f2eb1e9f907c9f" :answer/id #uuid "d074f739-fbb3-5d0d-a6b6-adbb55826957" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{10}{x}^{4}\\,{e}^{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-88586/selection/5d711dbe1837c5d640b4e6f4b565ce664a324df8a96f609cdd10a97b33d13853" :answer/id #uuid "3fbc2d0b-2152-5282-966e-613708b259ff" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-{\\int }_{0}^{5}{x}^{4}\\,{e}^{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-88586/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "69711ccb-86da-5dd0-b54c-611b81d4e05e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-88586/selection/d792654b44e68206c78ac4117abf07436eb5fad4aeedd5e393f659f1be21a56f" :answer-field/choices ["q-88586/selection/460d48d00f6d19174ffa7a6d5bddd5adc2a1dd496830c54e0b41a0757ee86cad" "q-88586/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" "q-88586/selection/d792654b44e68206c78ac4117abf07436eb5fad4aeedd5e393f659f1be21a56f" "q-88586/selection/129db039b7a10bb7c3f543c25e49869593eb89b9f23cc8eb06f2eb1e9f907c9f" "q-88586/selection/5d711dbe1837c5d640b4e6f4b565ce664a324df8a96f609cdd10a97b33d13853"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-88586" :question/id #uuid "8d29353e-115f-52b4-80fa-b9c7fdd3563f" :question/math-academy-id "q-88586" :question/problem "${\\int }_{-5}^{5}{x}^{4}\\,{e}^{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "Recall the following:\n\n- a function $f(x)$ is *even* if $f(-x)=f(x)$\n\n- a function $f(x)$ is *odd* if $f(-x)=-f(x)$\n\nMoreover, for any even function $f(x),$ the graph of $y=f(x)$ is symmetric across the $y$-axis, so we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-a}^{a}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=2{\\int }_{0}^{a}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nNotice that $f(x)={x}^{4}\\,{e}^{{x}^{2}}$ is an even function. Indeed, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-x) & =(-x)^{4}\\,{e}^{(-x)^{2}} \\\\  & ={x}^{4}\\,{e}^{{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =f(x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, because $f(x)={x}^{4}\\,{e}^{{x}^{2}}$ is an even function, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-5}^{5}{x}^{4}\\,{e}^{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=2{\\int }_{0}^{5}{x}^{4}\\,{e}^{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-88586/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2688742c-1655-557a-888d-af7e2179a89c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-88586"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-115278/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "12128697-5afc-509d-b095-b10903bdc8a8" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115278/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "da8bd8b7-b9b7-5c61-858f-19889bfb03d8" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115278/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "7fb54c0d-8e6b-5b2a-8326-ab4dd73e2d61" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115278/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "dd5beb10-d637-54e1-a007-9706a5d51ffd" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115278/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "3140949d-6243-520c-87d1-823e53d29c9a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115278/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "8aa056aa-e417-556d-9c3c-e03820513602" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-115278/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer-field/choices ["q-115278/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-115278/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-115278/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" "q-115278/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" "q-115278/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-115278" :question/id #uuid "3fb283e6-c950-59d4-b793-9a73d1c9314e" :question/math-academy-id "q-115278" :question/problem "Which of the following integrals evaluates to zero due to symmetry?\n\n- ${\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\sqrt[3]{x}\\,\\text{d}x$\n- ${\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x$\n- ${\\int }_{-2}^{4}\\frac{7{x}^{3}}{1+2{x}^{4}}\\,\\text{d}x$" :question/worked-solution "Recall the following:\n\n- a function $f(x)$ is *even* if $f(-x)=f(x)$\n\n- a function $f(x)$ is *odd* if $f(-x)=-f(x)$\n\nMoreover, for any odd function $f(x),$ the graph of $y=f(x)$ has rotational symmetry of order $2$ about the origin, so we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-a}^{a}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=0.\n$$\n\nSo, to determine which integrals evaluate to $0$ due to symmetry, we have to determine which integrands are odd functions.\n\n- The function $f(x)=\\sqrt[3]{x}$ is an odd function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-x) & =\\sqrt[3]{-x} \\\\  & =-\\sqrt[3]{x} \\\\  & =-f(x)\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by symmetry, we can conclude that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\sqrt[3]{x}\\,\\text{d}x=0.\n$$\n\n- The function $g(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ is *not* an odd function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g(-x) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-x)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-x) \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x \\\\  & \\ne -g(x)\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The function $h(x)=\\frac{7{x}^{3}}{1+2{x}^{4}}$ is an odd function, but integral III is not of the form ${\\int }_{-a}^{a}h(x)\\,\\text{d}x$ since the upper and lower limits are not opposites. Therefore, we cannot use symmetry to simplify the integral.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-115278/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3a247336-9bc8-5799-9956-e3de188ce2d2"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-115278"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186157902 :question/answer-fields 17592186156664] {:db/id "q-88686/selection/ma-v1/4543a1c3f10764ca70d14cf1ef27380fce5e861f0f99a33e4ba304244f3162b2/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "972c56a5-0720-5e47-b552-4d54d54b1a62" :answer/type :answe