4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-88686/selection/ma-v1/4543a1c3f10764ca70d14cf1ef27380fce5e861f0f99a33e4ba304244f3162b2/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" "q-88686/selection/ma-v1/4543a1c3f10764ca70d14cf1ef27380fce5e861f0f99a33e4ba304244f3162b2/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-88686/selection/ma-v1/4543a1c3f10764ca70d14cf1ef27380fce5e861f0f99a33e4ba304244f3162b2/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-88686"] :question/problem "Which of the following integrals evaluates to zero due to symmetry?\n\n- ${\\int }_{-2}^{2}{sin}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x$\n- ${\\int }_{-3}^{3}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x$\n- ${\\int }_{-2}^{4}4\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x$" :question/worked-solution "Recall the following:\n\n- a function $f(x)$ is *even* if $f(-x)=f(x)$\n\n- a function $f(x)$ is *odd* if $f(-x)=-f(x)$\n\nMoreover, for any odd function $f(x),$ the graph of $y=f(x)$ has rotational symmetry of order $2$ about the origin, so we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-a}^{a}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=0.\n$$\n\nSo, to determine which integrals evaluate to $0$ due to symmetry, we have to determine which integrands are odd functions.\n\n- The function $f(x)={sin}^{2}⁡x$ is *not* an odd function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-x) & ={sin}^{2}⁡(-x) \\\\  & =(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)^{2} \\\\  & ={sin}^{2}⁡x \\\\  & \\ne -f(x)\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The function $g(x)=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(2x)$ is an odd function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g(-x) & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡(2(-x)) \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{tan}⁡(2x) \\\\  & =-g(x)\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by symmetry, we can conclude that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-3}^{3}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x=0.\n$$\n\n- The function $h(x)=4\\operatorname{tan}⁡x$ is an odd function, but integral III is not of the form ${\\int }_{-a}^{a}h(x)\\,\\text{d}x$ since the upper and lower limits are not opposites. Therefore, we cannot use symmetry to simplify the integral.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-88686/selection/ma-v1/4543a1c3f10764ca70d14cf1ef27380fce5e861f0f99a33e4ba304244f3162b2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-334363/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "948a1765-e57e-539c-b9c8-bd22885976bb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334363/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "b07b79b1-be92-5d8f-8e98-b06e039938ca" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-334363/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer-field/choices ["q-334363/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-334363" :question/id #uuid "f865e8c9-95ec-5183-9343-bfa3396059b3" :question/math-academy-id "q-334363" :question/problem "Evaluate the integral ${\\int }_{-\\frac{\\pi }{3}}^{\\frac{\\pi }{3}}{e}^{{x}^{2}}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x$ using symmetry.\n\n${\\int }_{-\\frac{\\pi }{3}}^{\\frac{\\pi }{3}}{e}^{{x}^{2}}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Recall the following:\n\n- a function $f(x)$ is *even* if $f(-x)=f(x),$\n\n- a function $f(x)$ is *odd* if $f(-x)=-f(x).$\n\nMoreover, for any odd function $f(x),$ the graph of $y=f(x)$ has rotational symmetry of order $2$ about the origin. Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-a}^{a}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=0.\n$$\n\nNotice that $f(x)={e}^{{x}^{2}}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(x)$ is an odd function. Indeed, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-x) & ={e}^{(-x)^{2}}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(-x) \\\\  & ={e}^{{x}^{2}}(-\\operatorname{tan}⁡(x)) \\\\  & =-{e}^{{x}^{2}}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(x) \\\\  & =-f(x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, because $f(x)={e}^{{x}^{2}}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(x)$ is an odd function, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-\\frac{\\pi }{3}}^{\\frac{\\pi }{3}}{e}^{{x}^{2}}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x=0.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-334363/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ebbaf66e-6155-510f-b4d8-e38dd4c4f05c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-334363"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-334383/field-1/b0abf4f3840775218c55d4f317cb0c7770b27344c26735c40c11cc36b8f330c2" :answer/id #uuid "a7464299-3744-5439-850f-0f4d15492951" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-p" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334383/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "660520c4-7d1d-5338-b9fb-7abc302d1ec1" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-334383/field-1/b0abf4f3840775218c55d4f317cb0c7770b27344c26735c40c11cc36b8f330c2" :answer-field/choices ["q-334383/field-1/b0abf4f3840775218c55d4f317cb0c7770b27344c26735c40c11cc36b8f330c2"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-334383" :question/id #uuid "ef396766-744f-533f-88e7-0870256ee4de" :question/math-academy-id "q-334383" :question/problem "Given that ${\\int }_{0}^{2}{e}^{|x|}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x=p,$ express the value of ${\\int }_{-2}^{0}{e}^{|x|}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x$ in terms of $p.$\n\n${\\int }_{-2}^{0}{e}^{|x|}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Recall the following:\n\n- a function $f(x)$ is *even* if $f(-x)=f(x),$\n\n- a function $f(x)$ is *odd* if $f(-x)=-f(x).$\n\nMoreover, for any odd function $f(x),$ the graph of $y=f(x)$ has rotational symmetry of order $2$ about the origin, so we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-a}^{a}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=0.\n$$\n\nNotice that $f(x)={e}^{|x|}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)$ is an odd function. Indeed, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-x) & ={e}^{|-x|}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-x) \\\\  & ={e}^{|x|}(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)) \\\\  & =-{e}^{|x|}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x) \\\\  & =-f(x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, because $f(x)={e}^{|x|}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)$ is an odd function, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-2}^{2}{e}^{|x|}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x=0.\n$$\n\nFinally, using the adjacent intervals rule for integration, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-2}^{2}{e}^{|x|}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =0 \\\\ {\\int }_{-2}^{0}{e}^{|x|}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{2}{e}^{|x|}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =0 \\\\ {\\int }_{-2}^{0}{e}^{|x|}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x+p & =0 \\\\ {\\int }_{-2}^{0}{e}^{|x|}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-p.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-334383/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ebbaf66e-6155-510f-b4d8-e38dd4c4f05c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-334383"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-334381/field-1/b0abf4f3840775218c55d4f317cb0c7770b27344c26735c40c11cc36b8f330c2" :answer/id #uuid "a6186ac9-724b-59a8-912b-e8ec517e99ad" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-p" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334381/field-1/ec3dc34b21ac350807bcbba961b861de311aba9726d08b33967e6be5726343a1" :answer/id #uuid "83671361-543b-593a-a3be-530324db12af" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "p" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-334381/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "b7e73c3f-5c06-58e2-a94c-ab85fa9d40c3" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-334381/field-1/b0abf4f3840775218c55d4f317cb0c7770b27344c26735c40c11cc36b8f330c2" :answer-field/choices ["q-334381/field-1/b0abf4f3840775218c55d4f317cb0c7770b27344c26735c40c11cc36b8f330c2" "q-334381/field-1/ec3dc34b21ac350807bcbba961b861de311aba9726d08b33967e6be5726343a1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-334381" :question/id #uuid "907a64cf-d571-5ede-8004-0a234be6fa30" :question/math-academy-id "q-334381" :question/problem "Given that ${\\int }_{0}^{4}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{\\sqrt[3]{x}}\\,\\text{d}x=p,$ express the value of ${\\int }_{-4}^{0}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{\\sqrt[3]{x}}\\,\\text{d}x$ in terms of $p.$\n\n${\\int }_{-4}^{0}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{\\sqrt[3]{x}}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Recall the following:\n\n- a function $f(x)$ is *even* if $f(-x)=f(x),$\n\n- a function $f(x)$ is *odd* if $f(-x)=-f(x).$\n\nMoreover, for any odd function $f(x),$ the graph of $y=f(x)$ has rotational symmetry of order $2$ about the origin, so we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-a}^{a}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=0.\n$$\n\nNotice that $f(x)=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{\\sqrt[3]{x}}$ is an odd function. Indeed, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-x) & =\\frac{(-x)^{2}}{\\sqrt[3]{-x}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{-\\sqrt[3]{x}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{\\sqrt[3]{x}} \\\\  & =-f(x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, because $f(x)=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{\\sqrt[3]{x}}$ is an odd function, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-4}^{4}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{\\sqrt[3]{x}}\\,\\text{d}x=0.\n$$\n\nFinally, using the adjacent intervals rule for integration, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-4}^{4}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{\\sqrt[3]{x}}\\,\\text{d}x & =0 \\\\ {\\int }_{-4}^{0}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{\\sqrt[3]{x}}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{4}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{\\sqrt[3]{x}}\\,\\text{d}x & =0 \\\\ {\\int }_{-4}^{0}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{\\sqrt[3]{x}}\\,\\text{d}x+p & =0 \\\\ {\\int }_{-4}^{0}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{\\sqrt[3]{x}}\\,\\text{d}x & =-p.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-334381/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ebbaf66e-6155-510f-b4d8-e38dd4c4f05c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-334381"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-156690/selection/3791680ede9e6ad0418546e89942cbeb18b33314e97801c5f712c1db5778c3b6" :answer/id #uuid "cabc1eeb-9608-5e71-8f52-686ab9f527d3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt[3]{\\pi }}\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-156690/selection/ce77b8fa98d98857eafddec19fab178c965e986d1169bd85101c60f02365dace" :answer/id #uuid "cef42c49-bc5b-55eb-9d95-099a16363be0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt[3]{\\pi }}\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-156690/selection/7f3e3ccfc1490e67681aabff721f5de35a967cc2d83003d53b459776f4a62fca" :answer/id #uuid "a91ce62d-50ff-5e6b-8bd4-db84f4c3ee69" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt[3]{\\pi }}\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-156690/selection/389e6db3c0c5463f7402513112e5d0f9da2d7601f47a1746ca35045c3fb2cc18" :answer/id #uuid "dfd634da-f8ce-502c-8146-c98df7aedab9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt[3]{\\pi }}\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-156690/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "31bf39b8-f324-513e-86e0-acf8fd3305f6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-156690/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "38e291dc-eede-5cbe-8cb1-556d4ae6ff7e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-156690/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer-field/choices ["q-156690/selection/3791680ede9e6ad0418546e89942cbeb18b33314e97801c5f712c1db5778c3b6" "q-156690/selection/ce77b8fa98d98857eafddec19fab178c965e986d1169bd85101c60f02365dace" "q-156690/selection/7f3e3ccfc1490e67681aabff721f5de35a967cc2d83003d53b459776f4a62fca" "q-156690/selection/389e6db3c0c5463f7402513112e5d0f9da2d7601f47a1746ca35045c3fb2cc18" "q-156690/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-156690" :question/id #uuid "e9337ccd-0531-5f2d-96df-8781c1aaac04" :question/math-academy-id "q-156690" :question/problem "Simplify the integral ${\\int }_{-\\sqrt[3]{\\pi }}^{\\sqrt[3]{\\pi }}\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x$ using symmetry." :question/worked-solution "Recall the following:\n\n- a function $f(x)$ is *even* if $f(-x)=f(x)$\n\n- a function $f(x)$ is *odd* if $f(-x)=-f(x)$\n\nMoreover, for any odd function $f(x),$ the graph of $y=f(x)$ has rotational symmetry of order $2$ about the origin, so we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-a}^{a}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=0.\n$$\n\nNotice that $f(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}^{3})$ is an odd function. Indeed, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-x) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡((-x)^{3}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-{x}^{3}) \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}^{3}) \\\\  & =-f(x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, because $f(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}^{3})$ is an odd function, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-\\sqrt[3]{\\pi }}^{\\sqrt[3]{\\pi }}\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x=0.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-156690/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ebbaf66e-6155-510f-b4d8-e38dd4c4f05c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-156690"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
